.TH LOLCAT 6 "August 16, 2026"
.\" Please adjust this date whenever revising the manpage.
.SH NAME
lolcat \- rainbow coloring effect for text console display

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lolcat
.RI [ options ] " " [ files ] " " ...

.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page documents briefly the
.B lolcat
command.
.PP
\fBlolcat\fP is a program that concatenates files, or standard input, to
standard output (like the generic \fBcat\fP), and adds rainbow coloring to it.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
\fB\-F\fP \fIX\fP, \fB\-\-freq=\fIX\fP
Rainbow frequency: the hue completes one full revolution every \fIX\fP grid units.
.br
(at \-A 0 that is one rainbow cycle per \fIX\fP characters; default: 60).
.TP
\fB\-S\fP \fIX\fP, \fB\-\-seed=\fIX\fP
Starting hue in degrees (mod 360); 0 means random.
.br
(default: 0).
.TP
\fB\-A\fP \fIX\fP, \fB\-\-angle=\fIX\fP
Stripe direction in degrees: 0 = up (vertical stripes), clockwise positive
(90 = right = horizontal stripes); finite values within -360..360.
.br
(default: 71.6).  With \fB\-a\fP the angle is restricted to the
"down-right (but not too vertical)" through "straight down" sector:
18.4..=90 or 198.4..=270 (or their ±360 equivalents).
.TP
\fB\-B\fP, \fB\-\-anchor\fP
Color each screen cell by its fixed screen position, tracking cursor movement
in the stream.  Full-screen TUIs that only redraw changed cells (btop, htop,
...) therefore keep a stable color at every position instead of flickering.
.TP
\fB\-C\fP, \fB\-\-convert\fP
Convert between busyloop/lolcat's \fB\-p\fP/\fB\-F\fP and
CHT-1192/lolcat's \fB\-A\fP/\fB\-F\fP (float32 precision).  With no
arguments it runs an interactive prompt; otherwise give either
\fB\-p N -F N\fP (busyloop) or \fB\-A N -F N\fP (CHT-1192).
.TP
\fB\-a\fP, \fB\-\-animate\fP
Fade every line through an animation before printing the next one.
.TP
\fB\-d\fP \fIX\fP, \fB\-\-duration=\fIX\fP
Duration of the animation.
.br
(number of steps before showing next line; default: 3)
.TP
\fB\-s\fP \fIX\fP, \fB\-\-speed=\fIX\fP
Speed of the animation.
.br
(frame rate, i.e. number of steps per second; default: 60)
.TP
\fB\-i\fP, \fB\-\-invert\fP
Inverts the background and foreground colors.
.TP
\fB\-t\fP, \fB\-\-truecolor\fP
Enables 24-bit truecolor mode.
.TP
\fB\-P\fP, \fB\-\-pure\fP
Use a pure saturated hue wheel (hue 0 = red) instead of the classic
pastel palette.
.TP
\fB\-K\fP, \fB\-\-keep\fP
In the \fB\-a\fP animation, keep the input's own styling when a cell
freezes: background colours (or the input foreground under \fB\-i\fP) such
as fastfetch's palette blocks.  On by default; disable with
\fB\-\-no\-keep\fP.
.TP
\fB\-f\fP, \fB\-\-force\fP
Force color even when stdout is not a tty.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Shows lolcat version.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Shows options summary.

.SH EXAMPLES

Typical combinations of \fBlolcat\fP include other programs that generate text:
.br
.br
Make everything a rainbow:

.IP
.EX
echo "hello world" | lolcat
.EE
.

Rainbow fortune cookies are a classic:

.IP
.EX
fortune | cowsay | lolcat \-a
.EE
.

Full-screen animations work too (lolcat streams the output and preserves ANSI
sequences):

.IP
.EX
cmatrix | lolcat
pipes.sh \-p 10 | lolcat
.EE
.

For live system monitors use \-B so colours stay fixed to screen cells:

.IP
.EX
btop | lolcat \-B
.EE
.

